<title>JAPAN: Japan, U.S. to jointly study light-water reactors.</title>
<headline>Japan, U.S. to jointly study light-water reactors.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's trade ministry said on Monday that it had agreed to study the development of technology related to light-water reactors jointly with the United States' Energy Department.</p>
<p>Under the five-year agreement, the two nations will exchange information and experts, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Details of possible joint research themes have still to be worked out.</p>
</text>
